# Repo-wide ignores. site/ and site/supabase/ keep their own .gitignore for tool-specific
# entries; this covers everything that previously had no coverage at all, which is how
# .DS_Store files, Next.js/Wrangler build caches, and Supabase CLI state ended up committed.

# macOS / Windows / editor cruft
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
*.swp
*~

# Supabase CLI local state — machine-specific (linked project ref, pooler URL, tool
# versions). Regenerated by `supabase link`; must never be committed.
**/supabase/.temp/

# Xcode
*.xcuserstate
xcuserdata/
DerivedData/
build/
*.moved-aside
*.hmap
*.ipa
*.dSYM.zip
*.dSYM

# Node / Next.js — belt and braces alongside site/.gitignore, so a stray node_modules or
# .next anywhere in the tree (site/feedback/.next, for instance) can't be committed again.
node_modules/
.next/
out/
.vercel/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Env files. Anything with real credentials stays local; *.example is committed.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.gitignore

# Design-token sync workspace. Generated/vendored output plus its own local cache; nothing
# in site/src imports from it, so it stays out of the repo.
site/design-system/

site/design-system